## Build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

## Reqnroll's generated code-behind.
## Directory.Build.targets sends these to obj/, so this pattern is belt and braces for anyone
## building with an older Reqnroll or an IDE that regenerates them in place. Committing them
## means they go stale, and a stale code-behind is a test that no longer matches its feature file.
**/Features/*.feature.cs
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

## Test output, reports and evidence
TestResults/
test-results/
allure-results/
allure-report/
reports/
evidence/
**/evidence/screenshots/
**/evidence/recordings/
*.trx
coverage*.xml
coverage*.json

## Playwright
.playwright/
playwright-report/
**/playwright.ps1
**/.ms-playwright/

## Local databases (schema + seed scripts are committed; the built database is not)
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

## Local configuration overrides.
## Environment.Overrides.json is the only place a developer should ever put a credential, and it
## is deliberately never committed. Environment.Overrides.example.json IS committed as a
## template. Note this is NOT Environment.Local.json - that is the committed settings file for
## the "Local" environment, which is a different thing.
**/Environment.Overrides.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

## Secrets - defensive belt-and-braces. Nothing matching these should ever exist in this repo.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
!database/**/*.key
secrets.json

## Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

## Node (used only by the Allure CLI in CI)
node_modules/

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
